= Trades and Labour Congress

The Trades and Labour Congress is a Canada-wide central federation of trade unions, only the third attempt at the formation of a unified, national labour federation in Canadian history. It is a relatively conservative organization, favouring craft-unionism, and rivalled the more left-leaning International Workers of the World and the One Big Union in the 1920s.

- @tlc_relations: Improve relations with the TLC
- @tlc_organizing: Aid the TLC in organizing workers
